{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 2368, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nThere is a grid with 10^9 rows and W columns. The cell at the x-th column from the left and the y-th row from the bottom is denoted by (x,y).\nThere are N blocks. Each block is a 1 \\times 1 square, and block i-th (1 \\leq i \\leq N) is located at cell (X_i,Y_i) at time 0.\nAt times t=1,2,\\dots,10^{100}, the blocks are moved according to the following rules:\n\n- If the entire bottom row is filled with blocks, then all blocks in the bottom row are removed.\n- For each remaining block, in order from bottom to top, perform the following:\n- If the block is in the bottom row, or if there is a block in the cell immediately below it, do nothing.\n- Otherwise, move the block one cell downward.\n\n\n\nYou are given Q queries. For the j-th query (1 \\leq j \\leq Q), answer whether block A_j exists at time T_j+0.5.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN W\nX_1 Y_1\nX_2 Y_2\n\\vdots\nX_N Y_N\nQ\nT_1 A_1\nT_2 A_2\n\\vdots\nT_Q A_Q\n\nOutput\n\nPrint Q lines. The i-th line should contain Yes if block A_i exists at time T_i+0.5, and No otherwise.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\times 10^5\n- 1 \\leq W \\leq N\n- 1 \\leq X_i \\leq W\n- 1 \\leq Y_i \\leq 10^9\n- (X_i,Y_i) \\neq (X_j,Y_j) if i \\neq j.\n- 1 \\leq Q \\leq 2 \\times 10^5\n- 1 \\leq T_j \\leq 10^9\n- 1 \\leq A_j \\leq N\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n5 3\n1 1\n1 2\n2 2\n3 2\n2 3\n6\n1 1\n1 2\n2 3\n2 5\n3 4\n3 5\n\nSample Output 1\n\nYes\nYes\nNo\nYes\nNo\nYes\n\nThe positions of the blocks change as follows: (\"\u6642\u523b\" means \"time.\")\n\n\n- Query 1: At time 1.5, block 1 exists, so the answer is Yes.\n- Query 2: At time 1.5, block 2 exists, so the answer is Yes.\n- Query 3: Block 3 disappears at time 2, so it does not exist at time 2.5, and the answer is No.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n3 2\n1 1\n2 1\n1 2\n4\n1 1\n1 2\n1 3\n2 3\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\nNo\nYes\nYes\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 2466, "char_start": 2380, "quote": "Input:\n5 3\n1 1\n1 2\n2 2\n3 2\n2 3\n6\n1 1\n1 2\n2 3\n2 5\n3 4\n3 5\nOutput:\nYes\nYes\nNo\nYes\nNo\nYes", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 2540, "char_start": 2478, "quote": "Input:\n3 2\n1 1\n2 1\n1 2\n4\n1 1\n1 2\n1 3\n2 3\nOutput:\nNo\nNo\nYes\nYes", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "f969b0082712d25a633a837c71986ccf7b7789200161c1adf3f9102f89472aca", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "003c6a27aa3b53960318e52a2f84fa58396d2ee6a30e3196465925abf777f93f", "seq": 2}
